invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_field.h
catches: proof/prove-one.sh p256_wide_field
reason: p256_wide_fe_half adds p to an even element and nothing to an
  odd one, so the shift drops the odd bit and the result is neither
  half. The harness holds the halving to a reference that adds p to an
  odd value by a branch, and requires that the half added to itself is
  the element.

--- old
    uint64_t odd = p256_wide_mask(low_bit);
--- new
    uint64_t odd = p256_wide_mask(low_bit ^ 1U);
